&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item Description:&lt;/strong&gt; A DVD case containing the Australian DVD release of the Japanese animation film &lt;em&gt;Evangelion: Death and Rebirth&lt;/em&gt;. Whenever the DVD or its case come into and/or stay in physical contact with a person who is not aware of the existence of the Japanese &lt;em&gt;Neon Genesis Evangelion&lt;/em&gt; animation series, the person in question will immediately shout the phrase, &amp;quot;it all returns to nothing!&amp;quot; This phrase was subsequently determined to be a part of a song featured in &lt;em&gt;The End of Evangelion&lt;/em&gt; film, which is a partial sequel to &lt;em&gt;Evangelion: Death and Rebirth&lt;/em&gt;. The object&#039;s anomalous effect, in addition to the fact that the object was identified to be part of an Australian DVD set release that also contains &lt;em&gt;The End of Evangelion&lt;/em&gt; DVD, has led to &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;suspicions that its &lt;em&gt;The End of Evangelion&lt;/em&gt; DVD pair is similarly anomalous that, as of writing, has not been contained.&lt;/span&gt; the Foundation&#039;s discovery and confirmation of the anomalous nature of the object&#039;s pair, though it has not yet been contained.&lt;br /&gt;
