net/old-kansas-sector-part-2">Old Kansas Sector ~ 2: Tabloid</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/on-the-outskirts">On the Outskirts</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-first-sailors">The First Sailors</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/where-have-you-been-all-my-life">Where Have You Been All My Life</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/where-is-this-going">Where Is This Going?</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-26" style="display:none"> <p>Tagged k-class, but could not find a specific scenario.</p> <p><strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1238">SCP-1238</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-185-fr">SCP-185-FR</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1984">SCP-1984</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3274">SCP-3274</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4405">SCP-4405</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-736">SCP-736</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-770">SCP-770</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/shaggydredlocks-proposal">S. D. Locke's Proposal</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4742">SCP-4742</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/proposition-du-dr-gray">Proposition-du-Dr-Gray</a></p> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <div id="wiki-tabview-52b60dc5ece4f18bd451e4b4abe6579a" class="yui-navset"> <ul class="yui-nav"> <li class="selected"><a href="javascript:;"><em>Doomsday Contest Scenarios</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>ℵK/TPK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>ΩK*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>ED-K*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>K/O*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>MA*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>BE*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>GD*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>GR*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>ΔW</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>YN*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Project Palisade*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>☿K*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>MH*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>ARBH*</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Öß</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Other</em></a></li> </ul> <div class="yui-content"> <div id="wiki-tab-0-0"> <p>These scenarios were created for the 2018 <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/doomsday-contest">Doomsday Contest</a>. If you were a team member for a scenario, please feel free to provide a definition or otherwise update your apocalypse! (Also maybe double-check links, some of these SCP numbers were very similar.)</p> <p>Edit: Some of these (such as ΩK and EDK) have gone on to become part of extensive canons, so I have added links to tags for people who want to explore them deeper.</p> <p>*'s represent scenarios with 5+ articles on the contest page (Again, please update! I just used the hub out of <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">laziness</span>- expediency.)</p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: ℵK-Class &quot;Apotheosis&quot; Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/apotheosis-hub">Apotheosis Hub</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/apotheosis#pages">apotheosis tag</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 4 SCPs, 4 Tales, 0 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> Humanity (except those under Foundation control) is converted by an ancient thaumaturgic symbiote into god-like beings, later being destroyed.<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong> TPK-Class Thaumaturgic Proliferation scenario, אK-Class &quot;Foundation Apotheosis&quot; scenario<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3396">SCP-3396</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3731">SCP-3731</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3829">SCP-3829</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4420">SCP-4420</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-shape-of-a-gun">The Shape of a Gun</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-new-age-of-magic">A New Age of Magic</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-farewell-to-arms">A Farewell to Arms</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/thrive">Thrive</a> , <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/twinkle-twinkle">Though I Know Not What You Are, Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star</a>,</p> <p>Non-Contest Articles: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4568">SCP-4568</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: ΩK-Class (&quot;End-of-Death&quot;) Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/end-of-death-hub">End of Death Hub</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/end-of-death#pages">end-of-death tag</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 13 SCPs, 8 Tales, 2 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> Immortality is forced upon all life, without any other biological change.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3448">SCP-3448</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3984">SCP-3984</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4260">SCP-4260</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4935">SCP-4935</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3827">SCP-3827</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3866">SCP-3866</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4514">SCP-4514</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2304">SCP-2304</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4979">SCP-4979</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4725">SCP-4725</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4791">SCP-4791</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4206">SCP-4206</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/in-the-clutches-of-life">In The Clutches Of Life</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/omega-k">ΩK</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/societal-census-programme">Excerpts From The Societal Census Programme ΩK-Class Report</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/surgical-identity-perpetuation">GRANT REQUEST FOR THE PERFECTION OF BRAIN TRANSPLANTS FOR IDENTITY PERPETUATION AS TREATMENT FOR AGE-IMPAIRED IMMORTALITY</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/hypnotraline">'Hypnotraline' (TR7K2/2UD9X/53GN8)</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/with-the-reaper-on-retirement">With The Reaper On Retirement</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ii-tab-po-c-h20-qhs-prn-pain">ii tab po c h20 qhs prn pain</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-foundation-wants-a-robot-army">Tales Of The Ethics Committee: 5 Reasons The Foundation Wants A Robot Army</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-doctor-s-dilemma">The Doctor's Dilemma</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/project-damn-oh-fuck">Project Damnerung</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-3" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: ED-K-Class &quot;Lethe&quot; Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/amnesticization">Team Fuhgeddaboutit Hub</a>, part of the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ad-astra-per-aspera-hub">Ad Astra Per Aspera canon</a> (<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/ad-astra#pages">tag</a>)<br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 2 SCPs, 4 Tales, 2 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> A high number of ED-K Lethe Events occurring at a rate that both noticeably and negatively impacts human society and results in public awareness of the SCP-3848 phenomenon.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3484">SCP-3484</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3848">SCP-3848</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/excerpt-from-the-astrolabe-institute-journal">Excerpt from The Astrolabe Institute Journal</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/schulman-ny-programmable-mnestic-device-ac34d-nc77q-95dcs">'Schulman-NY Programmable Mnestic Device' (AC34D/NC77Q/95DCS)</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/paperpushing">Paperpushing</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/that-buzzing-behind-your-eye">Headache</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/when-the-time-comes-i-do-not-want-to-be-forgotten">Oceanus, Father to All</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/25-12-2047">25/12/2047</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-4" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: End-of-World K/O Failure Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/k-o-failure-scenario-hub">K/O Failure Scenario Hub</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 2 SCPs, 1 Tales, 2 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> Any scenario in which the Shark Punching Centre is compromised in such a way that it is permanently and utterly unable to complete its mission. Used by the Shark Punching Centre.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3760">SCP-3760</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/spc-001">SPC-001</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/peppersghosts-stupid-proposal">PeppersGhost's Proposal, I guess.</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/after-they-broke-our-fists">After They Broke Our Fists</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/spc-172-j">SPC-172-J</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-5" style="display:none"> <p><br /> <strong>Scenario: MA-Class Mass Animation Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/like-toy-story-except-fucked-up">Mass Animation Hub</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 1 SCPs, 4 Tales, 1 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> Everything with a face on it comes to life.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3406">SCP-3406</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/misery-makes-company">Misery Makes Company</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/artist-formerly-known-as-chuck">The Three Documents of &quot;The Artist Formerly Known As Chuck&quot;</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/uf-00031">UF-00031</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/serving-the-twin-cities-since-2021">Serving the Twin Cities Since 2021</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/chaos-praxis">Chaos Praxis</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-6" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: BE-Class &quot;Migration&quot; End-of-Consciousness Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/bird">Team Bird Hub</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/team-bird#pages">team-bird tag</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 5 SCPs, 5 Tales, 2 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> The replacement of a significant portion of human consciousness with an incompatible lesser mental state. In Team Bird, this occurred only after Thoth &#8212; a hostile avian deity who deemed humanity a fallen race &#8212; banished human consciousness as punishment and allowed an alien, avian meme to take its place. Later corresponded with the transformation of humans into bird-like abominations.<br /> <strong>Alternative Title:</strong> BE-Class &quot;Mental Migration&quot; End-of-Thought Scenario<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3662">SCP-3662</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3296">SCP-3296</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3362">SCP-3362</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3570">EE-3570</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3632">SCP-3632</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/join-the-flock">Join the Flock</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/tales-of-the-automaton-the-big-birdocalypse">Tales of the Automaton: The Big Birdocalypse</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/spc-507">SPC-507</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-sacred-djehuti">The Sacred Djehuti</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/avian-anthology-i">Avian Anthology I</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/umbral-migratory-sequence">UMBRAL_MIGRATORY_SEQUENCE.txt</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/avian-anthology-ii">Avian Anthology II</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-7" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: GD-Class Gestalt Dissolution Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/skies-made-strange-hub">Skies Made Strange Hub</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 1 SCPs, 5 Tales, 1 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> By using amnestics to try and prevent the exposure of anomalies to the public, these end up creating their own anomalies themselves.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3475">SCP-3475</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-quiet-night">A Quiet Night</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/into-the-woods">Into the Woods</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/hello-little-girl">Hello, Little Girl</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/it-takes-two">It Takes Two</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/children-will-listen">Children Will Listen</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/birth-of-a-new-day">Birth of a New Day</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-8" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: GR-Class Hostile Demiurge Event</strong><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 1 SCPs, 1 Tales, 3 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> N/A<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3457">SCP-3457</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/obskuracorps-memos">Obskuracorps Memos Acquired in Operation BLACK ROPE</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/archival-document-hsa-008-advent">Archival Document -- HSA-008-Advent</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-man-of-clay-and-men-formerly-men">A Man of Clay and Men Formerly Men</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/log-of-unexplained-locations/p/5#137">Unexplained Location UE-601616</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-9" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: ΔW-class eclipse-of-consciousness scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/squelching-blunderbuggers-hub">The Magicifient Squelching Blunderbuggers Hub</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 2 SCPs, 2 Tales, 0 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> N/A<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1798">SCP-1798</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3547">SCP-3547</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-slumbering-prince">The Slumbering Prince</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-long-game">The Long Game</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-10" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: YN-Class &quot;Ragnarok&quot; End-of-Knowledge Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ragnarok-hub">Ragnarok Hub</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 2 SCPs, 3 Tales, 0 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> N/A<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong> N/A<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3488">SCP-3488</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3378">SCP-3378</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/0-texts-found">0 Texts Found</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-curious-incident-of-the-contradictory-crocodile">The Curious Incident of the Contradictory Crocodile</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ragnarok">Ragnarok</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-11" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: The Threat</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/project-palisade">Project Palisade Hub</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 3 SCPs, 5 Tales, 1 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> A scenario involving The Threat, or THE WORM (yes it has to be written in allcaps, that's literally a thing in one of the articles); a multiversal entity beyond human comprehension that can instantly destroy universes, that may or may not be a discarded weapon from a war between even more incomprehensible entities. One particular iteration of the SCP foundation attempts to keep it away from their universe by making an uncountable number of parallel universes.<br /> <strong>Alternative titles:</strong><br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3818">SCP-3818</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3591">SCP-3591</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/wmdd-s-proposal">WMDD's Proposal</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/uiu-file-2017-003">UIU File: 2017-003</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/good-fences-make-good-neighbors">Good Fences Make Good Neighbors</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/daffodils">Daffodils</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/tko">T.K.O.</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/project-palisade-test-log">Project Palisade Test Log</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/in-the-end">In The End</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-12" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: ☿K-Class “World of Babel” Global-Incomprehension Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/last-light-hub">Team Last Light Hub</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 1 SCPs, 2 Tales, 2 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> A antimemetic cognitohazard meant for use as a weapon is accidentally let loose, causing all who are affected to lose communicative abilities, with words spoken as random gibberish or out of place.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3432">SCP-3432</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/not-with-a-whimper-but-with-a-bang">Not with a Whimper but with a Bang</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/kte-6024-blit-nuntius">KTE-6024-Blit-Nuntius</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/project-proposal-2024-258">Project Proposal 2024-258</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/pizzicato">Pizzicato</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-13" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: MH-Class &quot;Large-Scale Aggressor Overrun&quot; Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/war-on-all-fronts-hub#doom">War On All Fronts - Apocalypse</a> / <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/war-on-all-fronts-hub#anastasis">War On All Fronts - Anastasis</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 3 SCPs, 6 Tales, 3 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> Large amount of kaiju appear on earth and trample everything to death.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3534">SCP-3534</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5514">SCP-5514</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5391">SCP-5391</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/embracing-the-angels">Embracing The Angels</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/project-sensuikan">Project Sensuikan</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-kaiju-sea">The Kaiju Sea</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/storm-more-foul-land-less-fair">A Storm More Foul, A Land Less Fair</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/grant-request-for-mechacrocosquid">GRANT REQUEST FOR THE CYBERNETIC MODIFICATION OF THE CORPSE OF THE CROCOTEUTHIS GIGANTIS</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/awakening">Awakening</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/queen-of-the-monsters">Queen of the Monsters</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/critter-profile-cappi">Critter Profile: Cappi!</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/reviviscence">Reviviscence</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-14" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: ARBH-Class &quot;Insect Hell&quot; Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Hub:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/arbh-class-hub">ARBH Class Hub</a>, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/insect-hell#pages">insect-hell tag</a><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 2 SCPs, 2 Tales, 2 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> A scenario where any species or populace of insects, by anomalous means, becomes a direct threat to the human race and its environment.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3916">SCP-3916</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3879">SCP-3879</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4991">SCP-4991</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/critter-profile-genghis">Critter Profile: Genghis!</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/arbh-class-debrief-file">ARBH-Class Debrief File</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-morality-of-insects">The Morality of Insects</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-last-of-larpa">The Last of LARPA</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/zero-hour">Zero Hour</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/apologies-and-redemption">Apologies and Redemption</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-15" style="display:none"> <p><strong>Scenario: Öß-Class &quot;Multi-Universal Amalgamation&quot; Scenario</strong><br /> <strong>Used in:</strong> 1 SCPs, 2 Tales, 0 Other<br /> <strong>Definition:</strong> Interaction of our universe with another.<br /> <strong>SCPs:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3582">SCP-3582</a><br /> <strong>Tales and other articles:</strong> <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-small-town-in-arizona">A Small Town in Arizona</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/universal-collision">Universal Collision</a></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-16" style="display:none"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Title</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Articles</th> </tr> <tr> <td>XP-Class &quot;Reality Blue Screen&quot; Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/vending-machine-bug-report">Vending Machine Bug Report</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/how-to-make-a-focus-of-ultimate-power-a-guide">How To Make A Focus Of Ultimate Power A Guide</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>HB &quot;Beepocalpyse&quot; Scenario</td> <td>Anomalous bees infest the brains of everyone on earth.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3368">SCP-3368</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/i-don-t-want-to-bee-alone">I Don't Want To Bee Alone</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/what-if-people-were-bees">What if People Were Bees?</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2000-b-the-lonely-cowboy">SCP-2000-B</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>هلاك-Class &quot;Darkbody&quot; End-of-All-Worlds Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/dusk">Dusk</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/djkaktus-s-proposal-ii">djkaktus's Proposal II</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/dimensions">Dimensions 2, 3, and Onward</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Ϡ-Class &quot;Death-of-the-Mind's-Eye&quot; Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ute-9839-templum-ebbinghaus">UTE-9839</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Tashkent-Class &quot;Cross-Pollination&quot; Scenario</td> <td>Imminent alteration of reality or eradication of all human life is caused by the interaction between two anomalous objects of a radically different type.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/tuftos-proposal">Tufto’s Proposal</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-thing-at-the-bottom-of-my-dreams">The Thing at the Bottom of My Dreams</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>ZK-λ-Class &quot;Cosmic Fragmentation&quot; Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3426">SCP-3426</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/exploration-log-3426">Exploration Log 3426-UA-13C</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <div id="wiki-tabview-87d10805c032524bb87d45148d93867f" class="yui-navset"> <ul class="yui-nav"> <li class="selected"><a href="javascript:;"><em>One-Offs</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Joke scenarios</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Links to past lists</em></a></li> </ul> <div class="yui-content"> <div id="wiki-tab-0-0"> <p>Scenarios that have only appeared in one article.</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Title</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Articles</th> </tr> <tr> <td>AS-Class Normalcy Alteration Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3368">SCP-3368</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>AU-Class End of The World Scenario</td> <td>The result of testing SCP-475 with Australian Church of Australia's Religion</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-475">SCP-475</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>BB-Class Universal Formation event</td> <td>The creation of the universe in a 'Big Bang' scenario.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4417">SCP-4417</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>BC-Class Universal Collapse event</td> <td>The natural end of the universe in a 'Big Crunch' scenario.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4417">SCP-4417</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>DK-Class Reality Invasion / K-Class-Invasion-Scenario</td> <td>Entities from another Universe (E.g., Nazis) decide to conquer our Universe.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-int.wikidot.com/scp-028-de">SCP-028-DE</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>DT-Class Split Timeline scenario</td> <td>Rare (and non-apocalyptic) event in which the timeline branches into two parallel causalities. Most frequently caused by the malfunction of Temporal Distortion Engines.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3176">SCP-3176</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>EI-K-Class Informational Breakdown scenario</td> <td>One or more methods of information transfer become irreparably compromised.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3317">SCP-3317</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Gimel-Class Mass-Dementia Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3493">SCP-3493</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Götterdämmerung Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-319">SCP-319</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Inter-Reality Paradox scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3493">SCP-3493</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>MF-Class &quot;Spilled Milk&quot; Scenario</td> <td>Witnessed only in a dream. Based on the archetype of &quot;The Flood&quot;; a biblical flood composed of milk.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3739">SCP-3739</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>OK-Class Metaphysical Collapse</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4656">SCP-4656</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>PT-Class Paradoxical Time Breakdown Scenario</td> <td>An event where a harmful time paradox has occurred causing time and/or the timeline to be &quot;broken&quot;.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4255">SCP-4255</a>,</td> </tr> <tr> <td><em>Shin-Sophist</em> &quot;Global Religious Dissolution&quot; Scenario</td> <td>The subversion or dismantlement of humanity's religious institutions and dogmatic beliefs <em>en masse</em>.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4519">SCP-4519</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>class TCF (Total Contaminant Failure)</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2470">SCP-2470</a> <a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-1001-ru">(RU)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>χK-Class (&quot;Crowning-of-Death&quot;) Scenario</td> <td>The inadvertent containment breach of SCP-4260, resulting in universal supremacy of Death and the probability of life's continuation becoming approximately zero.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4260">SCP-4260</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>תK-Class Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/kate-mctiriss-s-proposal">Kate McTiriss's Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>██-class end of the world scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1000">SCP-1000</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>█K-class scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-453">SCP-453</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>ÞK-class Extradimensional Diplomatic Breakdown Scenario</td> <td>A powerful organization from another reality, having once been benign or neutral toward the Foundation and/or humanity, becomes hostile.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4587">SCP-4587</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Vaxt τ-Class &quot;Chronography Change&quot; Scenario</td> <td>A temporal paradox is formed, altering the present timeline due to actions in the past.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4437">SCP-4437</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>O0-Class Ontological Shift Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4634">SCP-4634</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>FK-Class (&quot;Broken Foundation&quot;) Scenario</td> <td>The destruction or failure of an anomaly management group, typically resulting in other K-Class scenarios.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4547">SCP-4547</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>UZ-Class Grey Goo scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/jack-ike-s-proposal-ii">Noir Box Proposal</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <p>Scenarios or versions that only appear in Joke SCPs. (I'm looking at you, SCP-666½-J)</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Title</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Article</th> </tr> <tr> <td>DK-Class Dominance shift</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-666-and-a-half-j">SCP-666½-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>RK-Class Rapture Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-666-and-a-half-j">SCP-666½-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>SK-Class Scorched Earth Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-666-and-a-half-j">SCP-666½-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>CK-Class Total Containment Failure</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-666-and-a-half-j">SCP-666½-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>UK-Class Universal Collapse scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-666-and-a-half-j">SCP-666½-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>URK-class you-are-about-to-be-killed event</td> <td>A scenario in which you are about to be killed.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-ttku-j">SCP-TTKU-J (which is a thing that kills you)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>UHK-class you-have-been-killed scenario</td> <td>A scenario in which you have been killed.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-ttku-j">SCP-TTKU-J (which is a thing that kills you)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>█K-class &quot;Dance of a Thousand [DATA EXPUNGED]</td> <td>Your guess is as good as mine, but it probably isn't pleasant, and the O5 council deems it bad enough to intentionally start an XK-class scenario in responce.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-100000-j">SCP-100000-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>scenario Alpha-K</td> <td>Unclear, but described as &quot;the-planet's-gone-to-Torture-Town!&quot;</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-900-j">SCP-900-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Scenario XK-OO1-J</td> <td>An entity known only as SCP-OO1-J is unleashed, leaving the foundation to enact pointless and annoying containment procedures due to The Administrator's misanthropy.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/daveyoufool-proposal">Daveyoufool's Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>TK-class Technological Collapse Event</td> <td>SCP-1938-J causes a global breakdown of technology by downloading viruses off the internet.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1938-j">SCP-1938-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>XK-Tweetle-Beetle-Battle-Breaching-Bottle Situation</td> <td>A Tweetle Beetle battle breaches beyond the boundaries of the Tweetle Beetle battle bottle.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-543-j">SCP-543-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>PK-Class &quot;Universal Consumption&quot; Event</td> <td>Winnie the Pooh eats the universe.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/djkaktus-s-proposal-j">Another djkaktus Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>AK-class Able-Demonstrate-To-You-What-Scaphism-Is scenario</td> <td>A scenario that Able demonstrates to you what Scaphism is.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-076-j">SCP-076-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>SCP-Jaguar-XK-End-of-Your-Lies scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-jaguar-j">SCP-Jaguar-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>BH-class salacious media scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1955-j">SCP-1955-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>BK-Class 'Total Buzzkill' Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/sparkle-spectacular">Sparkle Spectacular</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>RL-Class end of the world scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/this-is-the-real-life">It's All True</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>UK-Class (Unpunched Selachian) Beach Event</td> <td>A scenario in which there are beached sharks that have not been punched yet.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/spc-1981">SPC-1981</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>NOH-K Class &quot;Not On Hill&quot; scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/henzoid-crocket-s-proposal-j">Henzoid-Crocket's Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>MK-Class Normalcy Collapse</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-9999-j">SCP-9999-J</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>JK-Class End-of-Humor Scenario</td> <td>N/A</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-wow-j">SCP-WOW-J</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <p>These are past lists where people have either tried to catalog K-Class scenarios or made up definitions for them. Feel free to add links!</p> <p><strong>Descriptive:</strong><br /> <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/k-class-scenario">k-class-scenario tag</a><br /> <a href="https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TheEndOfTheWorldAsWeKnowIt/SCPFoundation">TVTropes EOTW page</a><br /> <a href="http://scpsandbox2.wikidot.com/k-class-scenarios">thedeadlymoose's version (sandbox)</a><br /> <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-225525/k-class-scenarios">Kapitano's version (forum, 2016)</a></p> <p><strong>Speculative:</strong><br /> <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-225525/k-class-scenarios">RhettSarlin and others (forum, 2010)</a><br /> <a href="http://scpfoundation.net/special-events-classification">Russian K Scenario List</a>, with both existing and potential scenarios.<br /> &lt;I know there is at least one (very old) A-Z list out there.&gt;</p> </div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/petrograd" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=455145&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608065511" alt="Petrograd" style=