				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5156</guid>
				<title>SCP-5156</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5156</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5156&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Euclid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5156 is to be contained in a Suppression-Exclusion cell, with dimensions of 10m x 10m x 10m. The interior and exterior is to be lined with 1inch-thick tungsten plates, each separated by 24 inches of concrete in solid form. The cell is to be only accessible by a series of three tungsten airlock mechanisms, each 3m x 3m x 3m. The ceiling of the cell is to be equipped with 4&amp;#160;30,000 watt Ultraviolet lights, one in each corner of the aforementioned cell. Only personnel with level 2 clearance are to be allowed to enter SCP-5156&#039;s containment cell.&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5156-01 is to be kept in a Storage locker approximately 17,000 meters from SCP-5156, while a Level 3 security officer is to be stationed outside the locker area at all times. Only personnel with level 3 clearance are to access the locker, with anyone attempting to damage or steal SCP-5156-01 are to be terminated immediately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5156 is a sexless,hairless,bipedal humanoid entity measuring 4 meters tall while standing erect. It has very little body mass and very little coloration in its skin, similar to SCP-096. The arms and legs of SCP-5156 is covered of abnormally large cuts and scratches, (of which would be fatal to a human) exposing the entity’s muscular system. The entity has no visible hands or fingers, but it is suspected to have perfectly invisible claws.&lt;strong&gt;(See SCP-5156 Testing Logs for more Details.)&lt;/strong&gt;. SCP-5156’s feet are replaced by stumps, which after close investigation it has been concluded the entity once had feet but have since been amputated by an &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;unknown source&lt;/span&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(See SCP-5156 exploration log 2 for more details.)&lt;/strong&gt;. On the back of the entity’s neck there is a symbol burned into its flesh, which has been identified as the aztec miquiztli, which translates to death; it is unknown how or why SCP-5156 received this mark. The creature&#039;s face is relatively human in appearance, though its eyes are sunken 2 inches into the entity&#039;s skull. SCP-5156-01 has 2 rows of human teeth, with abnormally large incisors.&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5156-01 is a large glass helmet measuring 3 meters in diameter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Addendum:&lt;br /&gt;
Both SCP-5156-01 and 02 were first discovered in __ Mexico on July 4th, 2019 after a series of unknown disappearances caught the attention of Maria Lopez, a level 3 Scientist for the foundation who was on vacation at the time. The following is a transcript of the audio logs taken during the investigation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4:30 am&lt;br /&gt;
Dr. Lopez: July 4th 2019. This is Dr. Maria Lopez, along with a native I will be investigating a possible anomaly located in __ Mexico.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5:27 am&lt;br /&gt;
Dr. Lopez: We have been walking for around an hour, in front of me is a strange pile of red ooze, I assume it is blood of some kind. In the distance I can see more of the piles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5:46 am&lt;br /&gt;
Dr. Lopez: I have started seeing things running through the forest, they are much too fast for me to fully see.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native whistles*&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Lopez: My associate has given me ear protection, may I ask why are these necessary?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Native: No good English, protect from screams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Lopez: Screams? What screams?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;screeching from behind *&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A loud thump followed by what sounds to be a struggle between Dr. Lopez and an unknown entity *&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Gunshot*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Dr.Lopez breathing heavily*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Lopez: Thank you Amigo. I was just attacked by some kind of primate. Hold on, it may be the heat getting to me but at first glance the creature appears to be a Homo Habilis. Interesting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;6:19 am&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Loud screams muffle Dr. Lopez’s words*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Audio Logs end&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Lopez later describes a strange Aztec temple, inside she found SCP-5156-01 chained to a wall, SCP-5156-02 sat on a pedestal in the center of the room.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5156 displays two anomalous qualities. At all times the entity emits a deafening scream, those unfortunate enough to hear it begin an anomalous transformation, which will be referred to as SCP-5156-02. SCP-5156-02 has been proven to not affect any other species. Exposure to the scream causes a human to rapidly devolve, this devolution stops at Homo Habilis. After 3 days any instance of SCP-5156-02 will explode due to unknown means, all attempts to prevent this outcome have failed. The only known way to silence SCP-5156’s scream is to place SCP-5156-01 on its head. Although SCP-5156-01 has no visible claws it has been seen making scratching motion over its skin and at the door, After examination it appears SCP-5156 is equipped with perfectly transparent claws capable of cutting through steel.&lt;br /&gt;
Three tests have been performed using SCP-5156-01. In each test SCP-5156 was subdued and locked to a large tungsten chair, SCP-5156-01 placed over it’s head. The tests prove that the entity is sentient, when shown various images the entity displayed several emotions, these include smiling, crying, and scowling. When shown a picture of the mark on its neck it displayed great amounts of shame, hanging its head and weeping. Dr. Lopez Requested a sketch of SCP-096 to be shown to SCP-5156, she was, “Curious if it knew who SCP-096 was, given the two’s similar appearance.”. Upon seeing the sketch SCP-5156 displayed extreme distress. The Entity shook violently and screamed louder than ever previously recorded, Noise sensors recorded over 200 decibels. The screams caused a large crack in SCP-5156-01. SCP-5156 shook its head violently, flinging SCP-5156-01 off of its head. All personnel present died later that week due to cases of SCP-5156-02. After the incident no further tests have been performed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/damien-loth&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7110198&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608065513&quot; alt=&quot;Damien Loth&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7110198)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/damien-loth&quot;  &gt;Damien Loth&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
